@@ -13,6 +13,50 @@ threadgroup-memory size. `agx_apple9.c` supplies those live parameters. The
 fragment importer, library parser, external loader and fragment exporter have
 been removed.
 
+## Opt-in G15 absolute target experiment
+
+`target_format` defaults to `AGX_APPLE9_LAUNCH_TARGET_COMPACT`, preserving the
+existing G16/G17 target bytes and callers. The distinct
+`AGX_APPLE9_LAUNCH_TARGET_G15_ABSOLUTE` format requires `shader_base == 1 << 40`.
+Its unsigned 32-bit `entry_offset` selects a 64-byte-aligned address within
+that fixed 4-GiB USC window. Misaligned entries, other bases and unknown formats
+reject the build without modifying the destination.
+
+This format places address bit 6 in instruction byte 2 bit 7 and address bits
+7 through 46 in bytes 3 through 7, little endian. Byte 8 remains a separate
+native control, zero for VS and four for FS/compute; byte 9 is zero. Successful
+native cap5 VS/FS captures and the qualified compute adapter are the comparison
+evidence. Private CPU tests compare the complete target instructions without
+using captured executable fragments in the implementation.
+
+Only target selection changes. This option does not select a device generation
+or qualify a complete G15 graphics launcher. The existing root loads, allocation,
+publication/frame encoding and preamble transfer retain their current contracts.
+G15 register allocation, stage roots and helper/preamble alignment still require
+separate native validation.
+
+## Experimental G15 compute wiring
+
+The opt-in `ASAHI_G15_COMPUTE=1` prototype requires physical G15, a complete
+608-byte GET_PARAMS reply with the known soft-fault feature and a valid separate
+USC window. Legacy devices retain the 592-byte params prefix and compact
+launcher. G15 keeps its physical generation; the checked profile selects the
+bounded Apple9 compiler and absolute target, without enabling direct graphics.
+
+The first compute scope is SSBO0 only, one writable buffer, local and dispatch
+dimensions `[1,1,1]`, with no textures, preamble, spills, shared memory, atomics,
+timestamp or precompiled helpers. Unsupported shaders fail compilation;
+unsupported helper or graphics submissions terminate with a diagnostic. Vulkan
+returns incompatible-driver. This is an experimental loader path, not complete
+GL/Vulkan capability support, and requires independent review before execution.
+
+USC allocations use the kernel-advertised window above the reserved aperture.
+Cached entries/free-list offsets remain arena-local; the wrapper's GPUVA and
+launch target use the actual entry BO address. Compiler bodies and inherited
+root/allocation/frame/helper encodings are unchanged. CPU checks do not qualify
+those controls on G15. Target acceptance requires the complete BO output and
+unchanged canary plus a signaled fence, since soft faults can discard stores.
+
 ## Independent shader entry ABI (T8132)
 
 Normal GLSL compilation produces complete VS, FS and CS bodies through NIR,
